

  # =========================================================================
  - id: S23-F194-bullet-cluster-clump-shape-claim
    date: 2026-09-03
    kind: superseded
    by: [F358]
    superseded: [F194]
    scope: >
      One sub-claim inside F194's Bullet-Cluster falsifier (section "The
      falsifier (E4)" / "Why the conclusion is robust"), NOT its conclusion:
      the statement that the QUMOND-type phantom-density lensing peak "can
      never migrate to the offset galaxies... regardless of a0, the
      interpolation function, or the clump shapes" -- stated as a strict,
      geometry-independent topological impossibility.
    reason: >
      Per the E13 reopening-condition protocol
      (docs/status/completeness-2026-08-20-prompts.md), a literature check
      found a live 2026 dispute working the exact QUMOND functional F194
      uses. Hernandez (arXiv:2604.10811, 2026-04-12) shows that because the
      phantom density is the divergence of a nonlinear vector field, compact
      point-like galaxy clumps versus diffuse gas CAN pull a disproportionate
      share of the phantom-density signal toward the galaxies despite the gas
      dominating baryonic mass -- clump shape is exactly the lever F194
      claimed was irrelevant. F194's own toy model used smooth, roughly
      Gaussian clumps and did not explore this regime. The strict form of the
      claim does not survive and is withdrawn.
    decision_ref: "F358 sections 'Physics' and 'Status'"
    findings:
      - path: findings/F194-emergent-gravity-bullet-falsification.md
        status: sub_claim_superseded
        dead: "The single sentence, in 'Why the conclusion is robust', claiming
                the phantom-density lensing peak can never migrate to the
                offset galaxies 'regardless of a0, the interpolation function,
                or the clump shapes'. This overstates the discriminator as a
                strict topological impossibility; it is not one."
        live: "EVERYTHING F194 CONCLUDES. E1-E5 all still pass and are
                unaffected (they are numerical results of one specific toy
                geometry, not the withdrawn universal claim). The bottom-line
                verdict -- the model-native emergent-gravity route is
                falsified and a dark, collisionless gravitating source is
                required -- is RETAINED IN FULL and is independently
                reinforced: F358 finds the MOND/QUMOND community's own 2026
                internal dispute (Famaey's arXiv:2605.10022 rebuttal of
                Hernandez) reaches the same bottom line by a different route,
                against the sharpest currently available (JWST) data."
        note: "Rubric row E13 stays EXCLUDED. CL168's falsifier field, unset
                when this record was written, is filled in by F358: an
                independently-verified baryon-only QUMOND/MOND match to the
                FULL kappa profile (not just the offset centroid) would
                undercut this exclusion; none has survived scrutiny as of
                2026-09."
    tests:
      - path: tests/findings/test_F194_emergent_gravity_bullet.py
        status: live
        note: "Do not mark. E1-E5 all still pass; the test computes one toy
               geometry's numbers and never asserted the withdrawn universal
               'regardless of clump shape' claim -- that was interpretive
               prose layered on top of the computation, not a checked
               assertion."
